### Biblical Truth. Pentecostal Faith. Spirit-Empowered Ministry.

Great Commission University of America (GCUA) is firmly rooted in the authority of Holy Scripture and committed to the historic Christian faith expressed through a Pentecostal and Spirit-empowered theological tradition.

We affirm the Bible as the inspired and authoritative Word of God and the foundation for Christian faith, doctrine, life, and ministry. Every academic program at GCUA is designed to cultivate biblical understanding, theological integrity, spiritual formation, and effective ministry in the power of the Holy Spirit.

## Doctrinal Statement

### 1. The Scriptures
The Scriptures are inspired by God and declare His design and plan for humanity.

### 2. The one true God
There is only one true God revealed in three persons—Father, Son, and Holy Spirit (commonly known as the Trinity).

### 3. The deity of the Lord Jesus Christ
The Lord Jesus Christ is the eternal Son of God.

### 4. The fall of humanity
Though originally good, humanity willingly fell to sin, ushering evil and death, both physical and spiritual, into the world.

### 5. Salvation
Every person can have restored fellowship with God through salvation: trusting Christ through faith and repentance to be our personal Savior.

### 6. The ordinances
We practice two ordinances:

**Water Baptism:** by immersion after repenting of one's sins and receiving Christ's gift of salvation.

**Holy Communion:** the Lord's Supper, as a symbolic remembrance of Christ's suffering and death for our salvation.

### 7. The baptism in the Holy Spirit
The baptism in the Holy Spirit is a special experience following salvation that empowers believers for witnessing and effective service, just as it did in New Testament times.

### 8. The initial evidence
The initial physical evidence of the baptism in the Holy Spirit is speaking in tongues, as experienced on the Day of Pentecost and referenced throughout Acts and the Epistles.

### 9. Sanctification
Sanctification initially occurs at salvation. It is not only a declaration that a believer is holy, but also a progressive, lifelong process of separating from evil as believers continually draw closer to God and become more Christlike.

### 10. The mission of the Church
The Church has a mission to seek and save all who are lost in sin. We believe the Church is the Body of Christ and consists of people who, throughout time, have accepted God's offer of redemption, regardless of religious denomination, through the sacrificial death of His Son, Jesus Christ.

### 11. Leadership and service
There is a divinely called and scripturally ordained leadership ministry that serves the Church. The Bible teaches that each of us under leadership must commit ourselves to reach others for Christ, worship Him with other believers, and build up or edify the body of Christ.
